family: line-cli
what: flow
transport: ipfix
address: 192.0.2.10
verification: reference
reference: common line-oriented flow export commands (flow exporter, flow monitor); RFC 3954 (flow v9) and RFC 7011 (IPFIX)
does: Exports the device's flow records to Woodshed as IPFIX (RFC 7011) over UDP.
check: Woodshed's Flows view lists the device as an exporter within a minute or two, with its templates and sampling rate.
placeholders: <FLOW-RECORD> <MONITORED-INTERFACE>
addresses: 192.0.2.10 2001:db8::10 logs-01.example.net logs-01
notes:
- Reference only: not tested on a device; check your device's documentation.
- Flow export commands differ more than any other here: some devices use one `ip flow-export destination 192.0.2.10 4740` line with a version keyword, some an exporter and monitor pair as above, some a policy that matches traffic first. Treat this as the list of values to set.
- The export version keyword differs too: use your device's keyword for IPFIX.
- <FLOW-RECORD> is a flow record the device defines (many have a built-in one with addresses, ports, protocol and counters); <MONITORED-INTERFACE> is the interface whose traffic to export.
- The template timeout (60 s) makes the device resend its templates every minute, so Woodshed can decode its flows soon after a restart.
---- part cli "": Enter in global configuration mode, then save the configuration
flow exporter WOODSHED
 destination 192.0.2.10
 transport udp 4740
 export-protocol ipfix
 source Loopback0
 template data timeout 60
flow monitor WOODSHED-MONITOR
 exporter WOODSHED
 record <FLOW-RECORD>
interface <MONITORED-INTERFACE>
 ip flow monitor WOODSHED-MONITOR input
